>
  <p slot="intro">Luci d'Artista began in the 2006 season and has grown into the largest event of its kind in southern Italy. These are not strings of bulbs over a shopping street: the installations are built pieces, often enormous, themed differently each year, and the city is laid out as a route you walk.</p>
  <p slot="intro">The twentieth edition ran from 14 November 2025 to 1 February 2026. The published calendar for the twenty-first gives the same dates a year on, 14 November 2026 to 1 February 2027. The comune confirms the switch on in the autumn, so check before booking around a specific evening. Our <a href="/en-us/blog/christmas-lights-sorrento-salerno/" class="text-med-blue hover:underline">guide to the Christmas lights of Sorrento and Salerno</a> compares the two.</p>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">How it works</h3>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">The route</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">From the Villa Comunale to the seafront</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">The main itinerary takes in the Villa Comunale on Via Roma, the cathedral quarter, Piazza della Libertà, Corso Vittorio Emanuele, the medieval Via dei Mercanti and the Lungomare Trieste. Further works sit in outlying districts such as Pastena. Allow a full evening.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">The queue</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">The Villa Comunale installation</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">The flagship piece is in the public gardens and is the only one with managed entry. On December weekends the wait easily passes an hour. Go early in the evening, or on a weekday.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</EventPageLayout>
